<title>UK: Tamaris buys Scottish nursing home.</title>
<headline>Tamaris buys Scottish nursing home.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nursing homes operator Tamaris Plc said on Monday that it has bought Lunan House in Arbroath, Scotland, a 41-bed home for the care of people with learning disabilities, for 1.1 million stg in cash.</p>
<p>The company said Lunan made a pretax profit of 202,000 stg for the year to April 30 1995.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
